  "label": "Economic Efficiency Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme implies that capitalism is more efficient than socialism by showing bread 'lined up waiting for people,' which is a stereotype that assumes market systems are inherently more efficient. This requires understanding of economic efficiency debates and the common ideological trope that markets are superior to planned economies, which is a real-world concept not visible in the image.",
